cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SubNetwork, please cite it as below. Its data is the work of the
  databases it is built from, so please cite those too: ChEMBL always, and the
  IUPHAR/BPS Guide to Pharmacology where you used its part.
title: "SubNetwork: a map of drug-target interactions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Szabo
    given-names: Attila
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/szaszeattila/SubNetwork"
url: "https://subnetwork.dev"
abstract: >-
  An explorable network of what molecules developed for neurological and
  psychiatric conditions act on: the proteins, how each molecule acts there,
  and how much published evidence stands behind each claim, built from ChEMBL 37
  and the IUPHAR/BPS Guide to Pharmacology. Exploratory and educational; not
  medical, dosing or safety guidance.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - pharmacology
  - chembl
  - drug-target-interactions
  - network-visualization
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The ChEMBL Database in 2023: a drug discovery platform spanning multiple
      bioactivity data types and time periods
    authors:
      - family-names: Zdrazil
        given-names: Barbara
      - name: "et al."
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    year: 2024
    volume: 52
    issue: D1
    start: D1180
    end: D1192
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkad1004
  - type: article
    title: The IUPHAR/BPS Guide to PHARMACOLOGY in 2026
    authors:
